course: dictionary
lesson: 10803
title: A medical word: varicella
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Varicella is the doctor's word for chickenpox. You will hear chickenpox at home and at school, but doctors, nurses and vaccine leaflets use varicella. You can work out its meaning from the words around it.
explain: «Chickenpox is caused by the varicella-zoster virus; spots become blisters and crust over in about a week.» The clues are chickenpox, spots and blisters. Varicella is the same illness, so it means chickenpox, an itchy illness that gives spots.
explain: Look at the word varicella-zoster. It names the virus, a tiny germ, that causes chickenpox. Swap in your meaning: «The varicella-zoster virus causes chickenpox» still makes sense, so your meaning is right.
fact: Varicella is a noun. It is the medical name for chickenpox.
fact: «Varicella» means chickenpox, a common illness that gives an itchy rash of spots and blisters, mostly in children.
fact: The varicella-zoster virus is the germ that causes chickenpox.
fact: Many children are given a varicella vaccine, which helps protect them from the illness.
fact: Varicella is uncountable, so we say «some varicella», not «a varicella».
exercise: Doctors and vaccine leaflets use which word for chickenpox? | Shingles | Measles | *Varicella
exercise: «Chickenpox is caused by the varicella-zoster virus.» What causes chickenpox? | *A tiny germ called the varicella-zoster virus | A cold wind from the north | Eating too many sweets
exercise: Varicella spreads easily from person to person. What does this suggest? | It cannot be caught by anyone | It is caused by a broken bone | *It can pass quickly from one child to another | It only affects grown-ups
test: «Children stay home until all spots have crusted.» Why do children stay home with varicella? | To get a free vaccine | Because the spots are fun to show off | *To stop it spreading to other people | Because school is closed for the summer
test: What is a varicella vaccine for? | To cure a broken arm | To tell a doctor how old you are | *To help protect children from the illness | To make spots appear faster
exam: Which statement about varicella is true? | It is a type of food eaten at breakfast | *It is the medical name for chickenpox | It means a broken bone in medicine | It is the name of a planet in space
